# D27 accept-both, SELF-HOST resolver lane: the canonical `^` move sigil in
# the NAMED-PARAMETER position (`Type ^name`), with the body USING the param.
#
# AXIS CELL: glyph = `^` (canonical) · position = named param · param TYPE =
# user struct (the sibling `String` cell lives in `d27_fmt_emits_caret.gg`;
# Core #12 "go TYPE-first" — this widens the param-type axis off `String`) ·
# lanes = Rust gg (C + LLVM), self-host resolver, self-host runtime.
#
# The `!` (retired-glyph) control for this cell is the EXISTING corpus — no
# new `!` site is added here, because `fmt_no_new_move_bang_in_migrated_corpora`
# (tests/lints.rs) is a shrink-only ratchet sitting at zero headroom.
#
# RED-verified against the PRE-port self-host resolver driver: this program
# yielded `DEF Variable ""` (the parameter's name was LOST) plus a spurious
# `DIAG error undefined-name ... `m``, and the `RES` edge for the body use of
# `m` was MISSING entirely. The `!` twin of the same program resolved
# cleanly, which is what made the gap a D27 accept-both hole rather than a
# general parameter bug. Post-port the DEF carries the name and the RES edge
# appears. Guards the `Type ^name` ownership predicate in parser.gg.
#
# Expected stdout: hello

struct Message:
    String body

String render(Message ^m):
    return m.body

void main():
    Message msg = Message("hello")
    print(render(^msg))
